@startuml
title D06 - Source-selection boundary and Project A member sampling
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif

start
:Source selector returns current index, p_source and slot;
note right
  Existing policy or independent Project B supplies this result.
  B includes its branch probability in p_source.
end note

if (Valid null / empty selection?) then (yes)
  :Return zero without retry;
  stop
endif

if (Published source index matches accepted UID?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Report publication/coherence defect;
  stop
endif

if (DTAL group / singleton parent?) then (yes)
  :Select real patch using member alias table;
  :Return p_member (singleton: 1);
  :Sample full-domain point and actual UV / mask;
  :Compute actual p_area (uniform triangle: 1/area);
  if (Outside standard-world point reach?) then (yes)
    :Return zero without retry;
    stop
  endif
  :dw = emitter geometry factor / p_area;
else (ordinary source)
  :Use existing source-type point estimator;
  :p_member = 1;
endif

:Trace actual visibility when sample can contribute;
:Accumulate history only for valid matching fast slot;
:Shade with 1 / (p_source * p_member);
:Include zero outcomes in the estimator;
note right
  No representative energy transfer.
  Area density is compensated exactly once in dw.
  No retry until the mask becomes nonzero.
end note
stop
@enduml
